{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum","lean:module:QOU.Mass.QDifferenceConfluentObstruction"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.shiftOne_const_residueSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.shiftOne_const_residueSeq","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L172-L179","doc":"For a constant-weight pure shift-1 tower the level index and the `t`-exponent lock:\n`r_n = cⁿ · a_{n−2}`. This is the sense in which the `t`-shift reading of #6582/#6610 is\na special case of the level reading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.twoOp_c1RecFrom_two_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.twoOp_c1RecFrom_two_iff","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L145-L168","doc":"**C1 on the residues from level `2` ⇔ index-shifted C1 on the `t¹`-coefficients**,\nfor a derivative-only two-term tower with `κ = c₁(−2) c₂(−1) ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.twoOp_residueSeq_add_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.twoOp_residueSeq_add_two","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L139-L143","doc":"#6498's residue formula in tower language: `r_{n+2} = κ · s_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.coeffOneSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.coeffOneSeq","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L136-L137","doc":"The `t¹`-coefficient sequence of the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.derivativeLike_twoOp_c1Rec_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.derivativeLike_twoOp_c1Rec_zero","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L123-L132","doc":"**A derivative-like shift-2 term cannot carry C1 from level `0`.** With `c₂(−2) = 0`\nthe first two residues vanish, so a C1 residue tower is identically zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.twoOp_residueSeq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.twoOp_residueSeq_one","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L115-L121","doc":"For the two-term operator the level-`1` residue reads the branch value through the\nshift-2 weight at the residue slot: `c₂(−2) · a₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.residueSeq_zero_of_powerSeries","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.residueSeq_zero_of_powerSeries","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L109-L113","doc":"The level-`0` residue vanishes on a power-series seed, for every operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.c1Rec_zero_of_init_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.c1Rec_zero_of_init_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L100-L105","doc":"Two zero initial values force the zero sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.c1RecFrom_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.c1RecFrom_ext","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L79-L98","doc":"**Rank two.** Two C1-from-`n₀` sequences agreeing at `n₀` and `n₀ + 1` agree from\n`n₀` on, for `q` not a root of unity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.C1RecFrom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.C1RecFrom","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L72-L75","doc":"The C1 recurrence `[n+2]_q r_{n+2} = r_{n+1} + r_n` demanded from level `n₀` on,\nin the geometric `q`-integer `qint`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.residueSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.C1KernelLevelReading.residueSeq","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/C1KernelLevelReading.lean#L68-L70","doc":"The residue tower of an operator `D` on a seed `X`: the `t⁻²` coefficient of the\nlevel-`n` jet. ","signatureChunk":0}]}